WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.500
Your electric bill went up again.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.300
Rent is due.

3
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.000
Groceries cost more.

4
00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:08.000
Something has to give.

5
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.300
So you ask it plainly.

6
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.800
Rates went up, and it's hard to make ends meet.

7
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:14.800
What can I do?

8
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.500
First, it checks whether you have a shutoff notice,

9
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.100
or your power is already off.

10
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.300
If so, that comes first.

11
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.800
Next come a few short questions:

12
00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:28.900
who your electric company is,

13
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.800
how many people live with you,

14
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.000
and roughly what your household earns.

15
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:38.900
If you're a Dominion customer in a family of four earning under $3,900 a month,

16
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.800
you may qualify for PIPP.

17
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:44.000
Your bill is capped at a share of your income.

18
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.400
Every month you pay on time,

19
00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:49.500
a twelfth of your old balance is erased.

20
00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:50.600
After a year,

21
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.300
all of it is gone.

22
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.800
Bring proof of income from the last thirty days,

23
00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.000
a current bill,

24
00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:00.400
and Social Security numbers for everyone in your home.

25
00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:03.600
Then apply online through CommonHelp,

26
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.700
or with Fairfax County Family Services.

27
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.100
Not a fit?

28
00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:10.400
There's still EnergyShare,

29
00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:11.600
a payment plan,

30
00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:13.500
or a call to 2-1-1.

31
00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.500
Asking isn't begging.

32
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.300
These programs were built for you.
